The `totalPages` calculation is incorrect when the number of users is an exact multiple of the page limit. For example, with 50 users and a limit of 50, it calculates 2 pages instead of 1. This results in an extra, empty page being shown in the UI.

The formula should use `Math.ceil`.

Suggested fix:
```javascript
totalPages: function() {
  if (this.get("user_count") == 0) { return 0; }
  return Math.ceil(this.get("user_count") / this.get("limit"));
}.property("limit", "user_count"),
```
